# .gitignore for the Professional Training course manuals workspace.
#
# The principle: track the sources a manual is written from, ignore anything
# the build can make again. Markdown, images, course files, settings, the
# stylesheet and the authoring commands are all tracked.


# --- Built output ------------------------------------------------------------
# deliverables/ is regenerated by build_deliverables.py from the Markdown.
# PDFs are large, binary, and change wholesale on every build, so they would
# bloat the history without being diffable. See the note at the bottom if you
# want a record of exactly what was handed to a client.
courses/*/deliverables/

# The HTML handed to Chrome, written beside the source document and normally
# deleted straight after. It survives a crashed or interrupted build.
*.build.html


# --- Dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
# Restored with `npm install` in tools/. package.json and package-lock.json
# are tracked, so the versions are pinned.
tools/node_modules/

# Python environments, if one is ever used here.
.venv/
venv/


# --- Python caches -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]


# --- Editor and OS clutter ---------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's slash commands in .claude/commands/ ARE part of this project
# and stay tracked; only machine-specific settings are ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Excel and Word lock files, which appear beside a document while it is open
# and vanish when it is closed.
~$*

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Uncomment if workspace editor settings should stay local.
# .vscode/


# --- Course material: deliberately tracked -----------------------------------
# courses/*/files/   hand-outs and workbooks - inputs, and small
# courses/*/images/  screenshots the documents reference
# courses/*/source/  transcripts and reference material the documents were
#                    written from. Tracking these is what lets another machine
#                    verify that a formula or prompt came from a real session
#                    rather than being composed.
#
# PRIVACY: the transcripts in source/ are Zoom exports naming every speaker,
# so they contain participants' names and what they said, for identifiable
# client organisations. That is fine in a private local repository. Before
# pushing to any hosted or shared remote, decide whether that material should
# travel. To keep the transcripts local, uncomment:
#
# courses/*/source/*.txt
# courses/*/source/*.vtt
#
# Note that git does not retrospectively forget: a file already committed
# stays in the history until the history is rewritten.
